 1. run([py, '-c', 'exit 0']).returncode; == 0             0; True
 2. run([py, '-c', 'exit 2']).returncode; == 0             2; False
 3. run(['definitely_not_a_command_xyz']) raises           FileNotFoundError
 4. run(['echo', 'hello'], capture_output=True).stdout     'hello\n'; True
 5. check_output(['echo', 'hi', 'there'], text=True)       'hi there\n'
 6. shell=True goes through /bin/sh: 'echo *' expands      'a.txt b.txt\n'
 7. a list skips the shell: run(['echo', '*'])             '*\n'
 8. Popen gives an object with a pid; wait() returns       int; 4
 9. after wait(), Popen.returncode holds it                pid matches: True; 5
10. run(capture_output=True): stdout, stderr, returncode   'out\n', 'err\n', 3
11. stderr=STDOUT merges; a piped stdout is buffered, so   'err\nout\n'
12.   with flush=True in the child                         'out\nerr\n'
13. run(...).stdout.splitlines(keepends=True)              ['1\n', '2\n']
14. Popen(stdin=PIPE, stdout=PIPE).communicate('abc')      'ABC\n'
15. run(input='fed') feeds the child                       "'fed'\n"
16. env={**os.environ, ...} is the child's whole environment 'hi\n'
17. os.execvp replaces the process: nothing after it runs  'replaced\n'
18. run(check=True) raises on failure                      CalledProcessError returncode=2
19. os.system returns a wait status; waitstatus_to_exitcode 1280; 5
